% ============================================================================
% seed-parts.query.adj — a worked recall over the biology seed-parts library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is the cotyledon
% for?" or "what does the seed coat do?": it states no botany fact of its own —
% it only `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine
% resolves each `?` against the `seed_part_role` rows and returns the role + the
% table's source/locator/trust. The fifth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind
% the role `food_storage`, recall its seed part — cotyledon). A word that is not
% one of these seed parts abstains honestly — the engine never invents a role.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli seed-parts.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "seed-parts.adj"

? seed_part_role(seed_coat, $Role)     % expect covering
? seed_part_role(cotyledon, $Role)     % expect food_storage
? seed_part_role(embryo, $Role)        % expect miniature_plant
? seed_part_role(radicle, $Role)       % expect rudimentary_root
? seed_part_role($Part, food_storage)  % reverse bind — expect cotyledon
? seed_part_role(petal, $Role)         % expect abstain — the petal is a flower part, not a part of the seed
